---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
    title="Projects | Cabe Robertson"
    description="Engineering projects by Cabe Robertson: MYOSA CrashGuard crash detection with AI emergency calling, EEG biopotential signal analysis, real-time face tracking with OpenCV, a self-navigating robot, and FPGA development in VHDL."
    ogTitle="Projects | Cabe Robertson"
    ogDescription="Computer vision, embedded systems, and FPGA projects, plus CrashGuard, an in-progress crash detection system with AI emergency calling."
>
<main id="main">
        <!-- In Progress -->
        <section class="section">
            <div class="container">
                <div class="section-head reveal in">
                    <span class="section-index">01</span>
                    <h1 class="section-title">In Progress</h1>
                </div>
                <p class="section-sub reveal in">Active builds, documented as they evolve.</p>

                <div class="project-grid">
                    <article class="panel project-card full-width reveal in">
                        <span class="panel-tag">Fig. 01 &middot; IEEE MYOSA 6.0 Finalist</span>
                        <h3>MYOSA CrashGuard <span class="wip-badge">In Progress</span></h3>
                        <div class="tags tags--accent2">
                            <span class="tag">ESP32</span>
                            <span class="tag">MPU6050</span>
                            <span class="tag">Sensor Fusion</span>
                            <span class="tag">BLE</span>
                            <span class="tag">Python</span>
                            <span class="tag">Twilio Voice</span>
                            <span class="tag">Claude API</span>
                        </div>
                        <p><strong>Selected as 1 of 15 teams worldwide</strong> in the IEEE Sensors Council's international MYOSA 6.0 competition, then <strong>1 of 7 advanced to the final round</strong>, presenting a live hardware demonstration at <strong>IEEE SENSORS 2026</strong> (Rotterdam, October 2026).</p>
                        <p>An OnStar-style in-vehicle guardian: ESP32/MPU6050 firmware detects impact events in real time from dynamic acceleration, then gives the occupant a ten-second window to cancel from a live phone dashboard. If nobody cancels, it autonomously places an AI voice call reporting identity, blood type, GPS location, and medical information, then answers the dispatcher's follow-up questions, grounded strictly in verified data.</p>
                        <p class="doc-meta">My role: Team lead, stack architecture &amp; test methodology<br>Team: Aidan Garcia, Jacob Randall, Cabe Robertson, Vu Ha Nguyen &middot; Mentor: Dr. Lavrova</p>
                        <div class="video-wrapper">
                            <iframe src="https://www.youtube.com/embed/vkzkJGDFFSU" title="MYOSA CrashGuard work-in-progress prototype demo" loading="lazy" allow="accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture" allowfullscreen></iframe>
                        </div>
                        <div class="hero-cta" style="margin-top:1.6rem">
                            <a href="crashguard.html" class="btn btn-primary">Read the documentation</a>
                        </div>
                    </article>
                </div>
            </div>
        </section>

        <!-- Completed -->
        <section class="section">
            <div class="container">
                <div class="section-head reveal">
                    <span class="section-index">02</span>
                    <h2 class="section-title">Featured Projects</h2>
                </div>
                <p class="section-sub reveal">Hands-on builds across computer vision, embedded systems, and digital logic.</p>

                <div class="project-grid">
                    <!-- Face Tracking Project -->
                    <article class="panel project-card full-width reveal">
                        <span class="panel-tag">Fig. 02</span>
                        <h3>Face Tracking with Arduino &amp; Python</h3>
                        <div class="tags">
                            <span class="tag">Python (OpenCV)</span>
                            <span class="tag">Arduino</span>
                            <span class="tag">Pan-Tilt Servos</span>
                            <span class="tag">Serial Communication</span>
                        </div>
                        <p>Built a real-time computer-vision system in Python (OpenCV) that detects faces and streams positional data over serial to an Arduino, driving pan-tilt servos to keep the subject centered at 30&nbsp;FPS.</p>
                        <div class="video-wrapper">
                            <iframe src="https://www.youtube.com/embed/a23yNcI4UtQ" title="Face Tracking Project Video" loading="lazy" allow="accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture" allowfullscreen></iframe>
                        </div>
                    </article>

                    <!-- EEG Signal Analysis -->
                    <article class="panel project-card reveal" data-delay="1">
                        <span class="panel-tag">Fig. 03</span>
                        <h3>EEG Signal Analysis</h3>
                        <div class="tags">
                            <span class="tag">NeuroPawn Biopotential Kit</span>
                            <span class="tag">EEG</span>
                            <span class="tag">Electrode Placement</span>
                            <span class="tag">Artifact Rejection</span>
                        </div>
                        <p>Recorded and analyzed my own EEG signals using a NeuroPawn biopotential kit, working hands-on with electrode placement, identifying and rejecting movement and blink artifacts, and working directly with raw biopotential data.</p>
                    </article>

                    <!-- Self-Navigating Robot -->
                    <article class="panel project-card reveal" data-delay="2">
                        <span class="panel-tag">Fig. 04</span>
                        <h3>Self-Navigating Robot</h3>
                        <div class="tags">
                            <span class="tag">Arduino</span>
                            <span class="tag">Ultrasonic Sensors</span>
                            <span class="tag">C++</span>
                        </div>
                        <p>Programmed an autonomous obstacle-avoidance robot in Arduino IDE using ultrasonic sensors, refining the control logic over repeated trials to achieve a 100% obstacle-avoidance rate in testing.</p>
                    </article>

                    <!-- FPGA Display -->
                    <article class="panel project-card reveal" data-delay="3">
                        <span class="panel-tag">Fig. 05</span>
                        <h3>Seven-Segment Display</h3>
                        <div class="tags">
                            <span class="tag">VHDL</span>
                            <span class="tag">FPGA</span>
                            <span class="tag">Karnaugh Maps</span>
                        </div>
                        <p>Designed a VHDL display driver decoding all 16 BCD/HEX inputs (0–9, A–F) on an FPGA board, optimizing the Boolean logic with truth tables and Karnaugh maps to minimize gate count.</p>
                    </article>
                </div>
            </div>
        </section>
    </main>
</BaseLayout>
